Given this FakePrefs code simulating SharedPreferences in DartPad:
class FakePrefs {
static final Map<String, Object> _store = {};
Future<void> setBool(String key, bool value) async { _store[key] = value; }
bool getBool(String key) {
final value = _store[key];
if (value is bool) return value;
return false;
}
}
Why is `_store` declared `static`?

Given this file read/write code:
final file = File(path);
await file.writeAsString(jsonString);
final content = await file.readAsString();
If `file.readAsString()` is called IMMEDIATELY after `writeAsString()` WITHOUT awaiting `writeAsString()`, what is the potential risk?

